palazzo with a heavy cornice, its centre breaking forward with three tall arched entrance openings, facing Washington Park across the street; the courtyard atrium and rear wing from Michael Graves's renovation (1989); and to the north the Ballantine House (1885), the brick and brownstone brewer's mansion with its porch, hipped roof and chimneys, which the outlines confirm. Turned 17 degrees to stand square to Washington Street. Guessed: dimensions (about 50 by 68 m, 19 m high), the window rhythm, the entrance arches, Graves's additions' extent, what the small outlines between the front and the street are, the garden's planting."}
